    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`-`  (up-directory) in  nvim.dir  is intercepted by a stale netrw buffer-local mapping, with behavior gated by leftover  w:netrw_bannercnt\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSteps to reproduce:                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                                                                                       \n1.  nvim ~/some/dir/README.md  (a plain file).                                                                                                         \n2. Press  -  (opens parent directory via the native  nvim.dir  explorer,  filetype=directory ).                                                        \n3. Press  -  again to go up another level.                                                                                                             \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \nResult:                                                                                                                                                \n                                                                                                                                                       \n• If the cursor is on one of the buffer's first few lines (in my repro, lines 1–6), nothing happens.                                                   \n• If the cursor is far enough down (line 7+), it does navigate up, but hands off to a netrw buffer\n  ( filetype=netrw ), not  nvim.dir .                                                                                                                  \n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExpected: navigates to the parent's parent directory, staying in  nvim.dir  ( filetype=directory ).\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1117+g4975a186f2\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nubuntu 22.0.4\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\ntmux\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ntmux-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from source",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-26T16:54:21Z",
