            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "My AI friend offers the following, which may or may not be helpful:\n\nEdit: it wasn't.  Hiding it away.\n<details>\nDiagnosis:                                                                                                                                                               \n                                                                                                                                                                         \n•  runtime/plugin/netrwPlugin.vim  always runs  packadd netrw  at startup (unless  g:loaded_netrw  is set) — expected, netrw still backs  :Explore /remote/archive paths.\n•  nvim.dir 's own  BufEnter  lives in the  nvim.dir  augroup, but netrw's  plugin/netrwPlugin.vim  (loaded after  plugin/dir.lua ) re-registers                         \n   BufEnter / BufLeave / VimEnter  in the shared  FileExplorer  augroup.\n• Every internal  :edit <parent-dir>  that  nvim.dir  runs for  - -navigation ( fs.lua 's  edit() ) re-triggers netrw's  FileExplorer   BufEnter  →  s:LocalBrowse() , which sets  w:netrw_bannercnt  and installs a buffer-local  -  →  <Plug>NetrwBrowseUpDir  mapping — before  nvim.dir  overwrites the buffer content/filetype back to its own listing ( directory ).\n•  dir.lua 's  set_maps()  →  default_map()  only installs its own  -  mapping if  vim.fn.mapcheck('-', 'n') == '' ; it finds netrw's leftover mapping and defers, assuming it's a deliberate user override.\n• Because buffer-local mappings always take priority over global ones, every subsequent  -  press runs netrw's  s:NetrwBrowseUpDir()  ( autoload/netrw.vim ) instead of nvim.dir 's own handler. That function no-ops while  line(\".\") < w:netrw_bannercnt - 1  (banner region), and otherwise performs netrw's own up-navigation — producing a real netrw buffer.                                                                                                                                                   \n                                                                                                                                                                         \nConfirmed via (read-only session):                                                                                                                                       \n                                                                                                                                                                         \n:echo get(w:, 'netrw_bannercnt', 'unset')   \" => 8                                                                                                                       \n:verbose nmap -                                                                                                                                                          \nn  -            @<Plug>NetrwBrowseUpDir   Last set from .../netrw.vim line 4888                                                                                          \nn  -           * <Plug>(nvim-dir-up)      Last set from .../dir.lua                                                                                                      \n:autocmd FileExplorer                                                                                                                                                    \nFileExplorer  BufEnter   *   sil call s:LocalBrowse(expand(\"<amatch>\"))                                                                                                  \n                                                                                                                                                                         \nCursor at line 6 →  -  does nothing. Cursor at line 7 →  -  navigates up but buffer becomes  filetype=netrw .                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                         \nSuggested fix: in  default_map() , before the  mapcheck  check, detect and remove a buffer-local mapping whose rhs references  NetrwBrowseUpDir  (netrw's own artifact from the reentrant  BufEnter ), then fall through to existing logic. Doesn't affect  <CR> /reload, which use unconditional  map()  already. Extend the existing \"coexists with netrw\" test in  test/functional/plugin/dir_spec.lua  to cover this exact  - -inside- - -navigation scenario.\n</details>",
