        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Apparently `nvim --clean` arranges that `dir.lua` is loaded _after_ `netrwPlugin.vim`; whereas `lazy.nvim` re-implements so that it all happens alphabetically.\n\nSo the code in `dir.lua` that clears the existing `FileExplorer` autogroup and replaces it with its own happens too soon under `lazy.nvim`.\n\nMaybe it's all a bit fragile and something can be done here, but I guess you can blame this on lazy.nvim",
