            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> `lazy.nvim` re-implements so that it all happens alphabetically.\n\nDoes lazy enable netrw by default, or is it something you specified in your \"lazy\" plugin list?\n\nIf a plugin is loaded, then of course its features are enabled. And if multiple dir-browsers are loaded, then... only one of them can win. So... don't enable multiple dir-browser plugins.",
