        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "as I said earlier - I guess you can blame this on lazy.nvim.  (I switched to vim.pack, feel free to close this out so far as I am concerned)\n\nBut is this working deliberately, or just-a-bit-better-than-accidentally?\n\n> if multiple dir-browsers are loaded, then... only one of them can win. So... don't enable multiple dir-browser plugins.\n\nit seems as though neovim _is_ loading two dir-browsers, and relying on the \"right\" one winning.  Perhaps this is not the most resilient design?",
            "created_at": "2026-07-26T16:50:05Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40965#issuecomment-5084442119",
