        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is a perfectly reasonable design. The loading order is intentional and documented; if a plugin (manager) wants to mess with that, there's nothing we can (nor should) do.\n\nBut I'm sure @folke can work around it now that the changes have a new unwanted side effect.\n\nAlternatively, `lazy.nvim` allows you to disable the builtin legacy plugins, which would be a perfectly fine workaround (and recommended anyway, until we yeet them completely). Try doing that.",
